<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tămĭăcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταμιακός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the imperial treasury</i> or <i>fisc.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedia,</span>”
				<i>crown-lands</i>, <i>imperial domains</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundi tamiaci juris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tămĭăcus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>an occupant of
				crown-lands</i>, <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11, 68,
			1</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
